@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+# cPanel upload — shuklatravelsindia.com
+
+Upload the **`public_html`** folder contents (not the folder name if cPanel already has `public_html`).
+
+## Steps
+
+1. cPanel → **File Manager** → open `public_html` of **shuklatravelsindia.com**.
+2. Upload all files **inside** this project’s `public_html/` (index.html, `_next/`, `assets/`, `enquiry.php`, `.htaccess`, etc.).
+3. Document Root must be `public_html` (addon/primary domain default).
+4. PHP 8.0+ enabled.
+5. Make `public_html/data/` **writable** (chmod 755 or 775). Enquiries save in `data/enquiries.json`.
+6. Point DNS A record of `shuklatravelsindia.com` and `www` to the hosting IP. SSL: AutoSSL / Let’s Encrypt.
+
+## After upload
+
+- Website: https://www.shuklatravelsindia.com
+- Booking admin: https://www.shuklatravelsindia.com/booking-admin.php  
+  - User: `admin`  
+  - Password: `Shukla@2026`  
+  - **Change password** in `booking-admin.php` (`$ADMIN_PASS`) immediately.
+
+Forms post to `enquiry.php` (HTML/JS → PHP). Email goes to `shuklatravelsjabalpur@gmail.com` via PHP `mail()`. If mail does not arrive, enable SMTP in cPanel or install a PHPMailer later.
+
+## What this is
+
+Pure **HTML + CSS + JS** (Next static export) + **2 PHP files** for enquiry storage. No Node.js on the server.
+
+## Next phase (later)
+
+Laravel CMS: login, edit every page, booking dashboard, then mobile app. This static site stays the public frontend until then.
