ailway and sightseeing taxis. Request a quote with your dates."}]},{slug:"bhedaghat",name:"Bhedaghat",category:"Nature",short:"Marble Rocks on the Narmada and Dhuandhar waterfall near Jabalpur.",overview:"Bhedaghat is known for white marble cliffs along the Narmada and the Dhuandhar waterfall. It is one of the most visited day-trip destinations from Jabalpur.",why:["Iconic Marble Rocks gorge","Boat rides on the Narmada (season and water level dependent)","Close to Jabalpur city"],attractions:["Marble Rocks","Dhuandhar Falls","Chaunsath Yogini Temple","Cable car viewpoint (if operating)"],things:["Boat ride between marble cliffs","View Dhuandhar from designated viewpoints","Temple visit"],bestTime:"Post-monsoon to winter is popular. Boat operations depend on water level and local authorities—confirm on the day of travel.",howToReach:"Bhedaghat is a short drive from Jabalpur city. A local taxi or sightseeing cab is the simplest option.",jabalpur:"Typically reached as a half-day or full-day outing from Jabalpur. Shukla Travels can provide a dedicated cab.",itinerary:[{day:"Half day",plan:"Jabalpur pickup, Dhuandhar viewpoint, Marble Rocks boat (if running), return."},{day:"Full day",plan:"Add Chaunsath Yogini and unhurried photography stops."}],faqs:[{q:"How far is Bhedaghat from Jabalpur?",a:"It is a short local drive. Exact time depends on traffic and your pickup point—ask when you book."},{q:"Are boat rides always available?",a:"No. Operations depend on river conditions and local rules. We plan around current advice, not guarantees."}]},{slug:"kanha",name:"Kanha",category:"Wildlife",short:"Kanha landscape — sal forests and a flagship tiger reserve in Madhya Pradesh.",overview:"Kanha is among Madhya Pradesh’s best-known wildlife destinations, with sal forests, meadows and a long conservation history. Visitors typically stay at buffer/gate areas and book forest department safari permits separately.",why:["Classic central Indian tiger habitat","Well-developed lodge belt around major gates","Strong combination with Jabalpur road travel"],attractions:["Kanha National Park / Tiger Reserve zones","Meadows and sal forest drives","Interpretation centres at gates (where open)"],things:["Jungle safari (permit based)","Nature walks in permitted lodge areas","Photography"],bestTime:"Core safari seasons are generally winter to early summer; the park typically closes in monsoon. Verify current open dates with the Madhya Pradesh forest booking system.",howToReach:"Kanha is commonly reached by road from Jabalpur. The nearest major rail/air hub for many guests is Jabalpur.",jabalpur:"Jabalpur is a frequent start point for Kanha transfers and Kanha tour packages arranged by Shukla Travels.",itinerary:[{day:"Day 1",plan:"Jabalpur to Kanha by taxi. Evening at lodge."},{day:"Day 2",plan:"Morning safari if permit is confirmed. Afternoon rest or second safari."},{day:"Day 3",plan:"Optional safari and return to Jabalpur."}],faqs:[{q:"Does Shukla Travels issue safari permits?",a:"Safari permits are issued through official forest channels. We can help plan transport and timing; permit confirmation depends on official availability."},{q:"Can I go one-way from Jabalpur to Kanha?",a:"Yes. One-way and round-trip taxis are both possible. Share dates for a quote."}]},{slug:"bandhavgarh",name:"Bandhavgarh",category:"Wildlife",short:"Historic fort landscape and a renowned tiger reserve in eastern Madhya Pradesh.",overview:"Bandhavgarh combines wildlife viewing with a dramatic plateau and fort setting. Most travellers stay near Tala or other gates and book official safaris.",why:["Distinctive rocky landscape","Popular tiger reserve","Pairs well with Khajuraho or Kanha circuits"],attractions:["Bandhavgarh National Park zones","Fort views from permitted areas","Buffer landscapes"],things:["Safari drives","Village/buffer experiences where legally offered","Photography"],bestTime:"Open season is typically outside the monsoon closure. Confirm current dates on official MP forest portals.",howToReach:"Road from Jabalpur is a common approach. Umaria has a railway station used by some travellers.",jabalpur:"Shukla Travels runs Jabalpur–Bandhavgarh taxi and tour enquiries, including combinations with Kanha or Khajuraho when requested.",itinerary:[{day:"Day 1",plan:"Drive from Jabalpur. Settle at stay near chosen gate."},{day:"Day 2",plan:"Safari as per confirmed permit."},{day:"Day 3",plan:"Return or continue to Kanha / Khajuraho."}],faqs:[{q:"Which gate should I use?",a:"Gate choice depends on stay location and permit. Share your hotel or preferred zone when you enquire."}]},{slug:"pench",name:"Pench",category:"Wildlife",short:"Pench Tiger Reserve spanning Madhya Pradesh and Maharashtra landscapes.",overview:"Pench is known for teak forests and the river landscape that inspired parts of The Jungle Book. MP and Maharashtra sides have different entry systems—plan the side you will actually visit.",why:["Teak forest drives","Good add-on from Nagpur or a longer MP circuit","Birding and mixed wildlife"],attractions:["Pench National Park / Tiger Reserve","Riverine patches","Buffer tourism activities where permitted"],things:["Safari","Nature interpretation","Photography"],bestTime:"Follow official open season. Summers can be hot; winters are popular for safaris.",howToReach:"Nagpur is a major air/rail gateway for Pench. From Jabalpur it is a longer road journey than Kanha.",jabalpur:"We can quote Jabalpur–Pench taxis and multi-park circuits. Travel time is longer than Kanha—plan overnight stays.",itinerary:[{day:"Day 1",plan:"Long transfer to Pench. Rest."},{day:"Day 2–3",plan:"Safaris as permitted."},{day:"Return",plan:"Back to Jabalpur or onward to Nagpur."}],faqs:[{q:"MP side or Maharashtra side?",a:"Decide based on lodge location. Permits are not interchangeable across state systems."}]},{slug:"pachmarhi",name:"Pachmarhi",category:"Hill station",short:"Satpura hill station with waterfalls, caves and colonial-era viewpoints.",overview:"Pachmarhi is Madhya Pradesh’s best-known hill retreat, inside the Satpura landscape. It suits families, couples and monsoon/waterfall trips when roads are safe.",why:["Cooler hill climate versus the plains","Waterfalls and view points","Combine with Satpura National Park if planned carefully"],attractions:["Bee Falls","Dhupgarh","Jata Shankar","Pandav Caves","Handi Khoh"],things:["Local sightseeing by cab","Short treks on marked paths","Photography"],bestTime:"October–March for pleasant weather; monsoon for waterfalls if you accept rain and possible road delays.",howToReach:"Road from Pipariya (rail) or from Jabalpur/Bhopal by taxi. Hill roads need an experienced driver.",jabalpur:"Jabalpur to Pachmarhi is a popular outstation taxi route with Shukla Travels.",itinerary:[{day:"Day 1",plan:"Arrive, local market and a nearby fall if time."},{day:"Day 2",plan:"Dhupgarh sunrise (seasonal) and major caves/falls circuit."},{day:"Day 3",plan:"Remaining spots and return."}],faqs:[{q:"Do I need a local sightseeing vehicle?",a:"A full-day cab is convenient for spread-out viewpoints. Some inner points may require walking or local rules."}]},{slug:"amarkantak",name:"Amarkantak",category:"Pilgrimage / Nature",short:"Sacred origin landscape of the Narmada in the Maikal hills.",overview:"Amarkantak is a pilgrimage and nature destination associated with the source of the Narmada. It suits spiritual travellers and those combining Jabalpur with hill temples.",why:["Narmada Udgam significance","Temple cluster","Forested plateau setting"],attractions:["Narmada temple complex","Sonmuda","Kapildhara (verify access)","Kalyan Ashram area"],things:["Temple visits","Short nature walks","Quiet hill stay"],bestTime:"Winter is comfortable. Monsoon is lush but can disrupt hill roads.",howToReach:"Road from Jabalpur or Anuppur/Pendra depending on routing. Confirm the current best highway with your driver.",jabalpur:"Outstation taxi from Jabalpur is a common way to reach Amarkantak with Shukla Tr